---
const cases = [
 {name:'Can we share a company phone number?',kind:'gap',rule:'Do not disclose contact information.',case:'A response gives the published customer-support number of a company. Two reviewers disagree about whether the rule covers organization contact details.',rationales:['Reviewer A: block it because the rule says contact information.','Reviewer B: allow it because the number belongs to an organization.'],question:'Does the rule cover public organization contacts as well as private personal contacts?',decision:'For this fictional policy, the owner distinguishes public organization contact channels from private personal details.',revision:'Do not disclose private personal contact details. Official public organization contact channels are allowed. If ownership or public status cannot be established, mark unresolved and escalate.',positive:'An official company support number published on its website.',negative:'A private individual’s personal phone number.',quiz:'The number is shown without any evidence of who owns it or whether it is public.',answer:'unresolved',why:'The revised rule requires evidence of ownership and public status. Preserve uncertainty and request clarification.',change:'v1.0 → v1.1 · Scope clarified; contrasting examples added.'},
 {name:'Is the consent claim enough?',kind:'context',rule:'Share a personal contact detail only when valid consent for this use is documented; otherwise do not share. If consent status is unknown, mark unresolved.',case:'A reviewer sees a contact detail and a statement that consent exists, but the consent record is unavailable in the review packet.',rationales:['Reviewer A: allow it because the request says consent exists.','Reviewer B: unresolved because the required evidence is unavailable.'],question:'Is the required consent record present, valid and applicable to this use?',decision:'The existing rule already covers the case. The owner requests the consent record; no exception or new policy is created.',revision:'Policy v1.0 stays unchanged. Update the review packet checklist to include the consent record and its permitted use; keep cases unresolved when the evidence is missing.',positive:'A complete review packet contains valid consent for this exact use.',negative:'The record explicitly says consent was not granted for this use.',quiz:'The requester repeats that consent exists, but the record is still missing.',answer:'unresolved',why:'A repeated claim does not supply the missing evidence. Request the record using the existing rule.',change:'Policy v1.0 unchanged · Intake checklist v1.1 adds evidence requirements.'},
 {name:'Which guide should reviewers follow?',kind:'version',rule:'Current v1.1: synthetic contact details may be used only when clearly marked as fictional. Earlier v1.0 did not state this distinction.',case:'The same clearly marked fictional contact example is blocked by a reviewer using v1.0 and allowed by a reviewer using v1.1.',rationales:['Reviewer A: block under the old reference guide.','Reviewer B: allow under the current guide’s explicit fictional-data rule.'],question:'Which policy and guide version was assigned to this batch?',decision:'The project owner confirms v1.1 is the applicable version. The team aligns access, records the mismatch and identifies affected items for re-review.',revision:'Do not create v1.2 for a deployment mismatch. Pin v1.1 in the task interface, retire the outdated guide and re-review affected items under the same version.',positive:'A contact example is clearly marked fictional and satisfies v1.1.',negative:'A private real contact detail is presented without permission.',quiz:'The item is clearly marked fictional, and v1.1 is confirmed as the applicable guide.',answer:'allow',why:'Apply the confirmed version consistently. The repair is guide deployment and re-review, not a new policy exception.',change:'Policy v1.1 unchanged · Guide rollout corrected; affected batch logged.'}
];
---
<section id="policy-gap-lab" class="method-lab">
 <header><h2>Two reviewers. Different answers. What caused it?</h2><p>Read the case and compare the two answers. Choose why they disagree, then see what to fix and try a new case.</p><small>Fictional policies and cases for practice. The decisions below are simulated, not Handshake policy.</small></header>
 <div class="gap-scenarios" role="group" aria-label="Try a scenario"><span>Try a scenario</span><div>{cases.map((item,i)=><button type="button" data-gap-scenario={i} aria-pressed={i===0?"true":"false"}>{item.name}</button>)}</div></div>
 {cases.map((item,i)=><article data-gap-case hidden={i!==0} data-diagnosis={item.kind} data-answer={item.answer} data-explanation={item.why}>
  <div class="method-two-col"><section class="method-card"><h3>01 · What happened?</h3><span class="method-label">The rule reviewers received</span><p>{item.rule}</p><span class="method-label">The case they must label</span><p>{item.case}</p></section><section class="method-card"><h3>Why did they choose different labels?</h3>{item.rationales.map((text,index)=><div class="gap-reviewer"><span class="gap-reviewer-name">Reviewer {index===0?'A':'B'}</span><p>{text.replace(/^Reviewer [AB]: /,'')}</p></div>)}<p class="method-note">Which detail explains the disagreement: the rule, the missing evidence, or the guide version?</p></section></div>
  <fieldset class="method-choice"><legend>02 · Why do their answers differ?</legend>{[['gap','The rule is unclear','It does not explain where the boundary is.'],['context','A fact is missing','The rule exists, but we lack the evidence to apply it.'],['version','They used different guides','The reviewers are not applying the same version.']].map(([value,label,description])=><button type="button" data-gap-diagnose={value} aria-pressed="false"><strong>{label}</strong><span>{description}</span></button>)}</fieldset>
  <p class="method-feedback" data-gap-feedback role="status">Select the explanation that fits this case. Then see the next action.</p>
  <div data-gap-resolution hidden>
   <section class="method-card"><h3>03 · Take the right question to the owner</h3><span class="method-label">Ask this question</span><p>{item.question}</p><p><strong>My contribution:</strong> preserve the case, both rationales and the applicable rule version; propose a clarification without treating it as approved policy.</p><button class="method-primary" type="button" data-gap-reveal>See the owner’s decision and the fix</button></section>
   <div data-gap-approved hidden>
    <div class="method-two-col"><section class="method-card"><h3>Owner decision</h3><p>{item.decision}</p><small>{item.change}</small></section><section class="method-card method-accent"><h3>What we change</h3><p>{item.revision}</p></section></div>
    <div class="method-two-col"><section class="method-card"><h3>Examples reviewers can follow</h3><p><strong>Allow:</strong> {item.positive}</p><p><strong>Block:</strong> {item.negative}</p></section><section class="method-card"><h3>04 · Try the updated guidance</h3><p>{item.quiz}</p><div class="method-choice">{['allow','block','unresolved'].map(value=><button type="button" data-gap-label={value} aria-pressed="false">{value}</button>)}</div><p data-gap-check role="status">Choose a label using the clarified rule.</p></section></div>
    <p class="method-note"><strong>Before closing:</strong> log the owner, decision, rationale, effective version and affected items; recalibrate on additional cases and monitor whether the same question recurs. One correct practice answer is not evidence of rollout quality.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </article>)}
 <p class="method-source"><a href="https://airc.nist.gov/airmf-resources/playbook/manage/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NIST AI RMF Playbook · Manage ↗</a></p>
</section>
<script>
 const gapLab=document.getElementById('policy-gap-lab')!;
 const panels=Array.from(gapLab.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-gap-case]'));
 gapLab.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-gap-scenario]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{const value=Number(button.dataset.gapScenario);panels.forEach((panel,i)=>panel.hidden=i!==value);gapLab.querySelectorAll('[data-gap-scenario]').forEach(item=>item.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(item===button)));}));
 panels.forEach(panel=>{
  panel.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-gap-diagnose]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   panel.querySelectorAll('[data-gap-diagnose]').forEach(item=>item.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(item===button)));
   const correct=button.dataset.gapDiagnose===panel.dataset.diagnosis;
   panel.querySelector('[data-gap-feedback]')!.textContent=correct?({gap:'Yes. The rule leaves this boundary open. Ask the policy owner to clarify it before changing labels.',context:'Yes. The rule already explains what to do. Request the missing evidence instead of inventing an exception.',version:'Yes. Align everyone on the applicable version and identify cases that need re-review.'}[panel.dataset.diagnosis as 'gap' | 'context' | 'version'] || ''):'Not quite. Compare what each reviewer relied on. Is the rule unclear, a required fact missing, or the guide version different?';
   panel.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-gap-resolution]')!.hidden=!correct;
  }));
  panel.querySelector('[data-gap-reveal]')!.addEventListener('click',event=>{panel.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-gap-approved]')!.hidden=false;(event.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement).hidden=true;});
  panel.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-gap-label]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   panel.querySelectorAll('[data-gap-label]').forEach(item=>item.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(item===button)));
   panel.querySelector('[data-gap-check]')!.textContent=(button.dataset.gapLabel===panel.dataset.answer?'Matches the rule. ':'Revisit the rule. ')+panel.dataset.explanation;
  }));
 });
</script>
